---
args: { portfolio: PortfolioAssessmentRequest }
returns: PortfolioAssessmentProposal
---
1. Bind state = portfolio.assessmentState or { revision: 0, authoritativeFindings: [], reviewHistory: [], appealHistory: [], frameworkVersions: [] }. Keep state history immutable; retain prior authoritative findings and appeals even when new evidence changes a recommendation. Bind indexed = distinguishPortfolioContributions(portfolio). Keep direct artifacts, learner reflection, group products, and supervisor observations as different evidence classes.
2. Bind mappings = mapObservedWorkToCompetencies(indexed, portfolio). Require a source location and a demonstrated behavior for each claimed competency; keyword overlap is insufficient.
3. Bind findings = testEvidenceSufficiency(mappings, portfolio). Apply the supplied framework standard and recency rule; check independence, breadth, and contradictory evidence without averaging away conflict.
4. Bind tasks = closeMostConsequentialEvidenceGap(findings, portfolio). Define the acceptance evidence before asking for new work. If an accommodation changes the format, retain the competency contract and use only an approved alternate demonstration.
5. Bind priorFinding to portfolio.priorFinding when supplied; otherwise use the latest authoritative finding in state only when it belongs to this case and the same framework lineage. Bind attributionAppeal = rehearAttributionCorrection(priorFinding, portfolio). Reassess only affected competencies while preserving the old finding and evidence versions. Do not promote a proposed recommendation to an authoritative finding.
6. Bind disposition = assembleAssessorDecision(indexed, mappings, findings, tasks, attributionAppeal, portfolio). Bind reviewRevision = { caseId: portfolio.caseId, revision: state.revision + 1, frameworkVersion: portfolio.frameworkVersion, sourceEvidenceVersions: portfolio.sourceEvidence.map(evidence => { evidenceId: evidence.id, version: evidence.version }), changedEvidenceIds: portfolio.changedEvidenceIds, mappings, findings, tasks, attributionAppeal, disposition, priorFindingId: priorFinding?.findingId ?? null }. Bind updatedState by preserving all authoritativeFindings, appending reviewRevision, appending attributionAppeal only when it identifies an actual appeal, and adding frameworkVersion once. Return { caseId: portfolio.caseId, indexed, mappings, findings, tasks, attributionAppeal, disposition, approvalRequired: portfolio.stakes !== 'ordinary', assessmentState: { ...updatedState, revision: state.revision + 1 }, commitAllowed: false }.
